module gunbc.recurring_failure_mode.a_declared_container_type_is_checked_by_head_only

import std.types { NonEmptyStr }
import gunbc.recurring_failure_mode { BelowCeiling, FoundBelowTheLadder, RecurringFailureMode, RungRead }
import gunbc.guarantee_rung { StructurallyGuaranteed }
import gunbc.rung_climb { ClimbableButUnbuilt }

data a_declared_container_type_is_checked_by_head_only: RecurringFailureMode = RecurringFailureMode {
  identity: "a_declared_container_type_is_checked_by_head_only" as NonEmptyStr,

  rung: RungRead { found_at: FoundBelowTheLadder, standing: BelowCeiling { current: FoundBelowTheLadder, ceiling: StructurallyGuaranteed, blocker: ClimbableButUnbuilt, trigger_capability: "the capability of judging a declared container application against a produced one at every type-argument position, recursively, with a position holding an unsolved variable undecided rather than agreeing, so no Accepted program binds a value whose container type disagrees with its declaration at any argument." } },

  receipts: [
    "**a declared container type is checked by its head only** (a value whose container type disagrees with its declaration at some type-argument position is accepted, because the declared-position judgment compares the container's head, or at most its first argument one level down).",

    "INVALID STATE: an Accepted program in which a binder, return, field or argument declared Map<K1, V1> (or List<List<A>>) holds a value of Map<K2, V2> (or List<List<B>>) with K1 /= K2 or V1 /= V2 (A /= B).",

    "HARM: silent wrongness. The emitted Rust drops the annotation (`let q: Map<Bool, Bool> = m` emits `let q = m.clone();`), so rustc has nothing to refuse either, and the wrong type surfaces at the first consumer that reads the value as its declared type.",

    "SPECIMEN (srv1, v1 seed built from main 8de219bdc5ad, 2026-10-30): `let m: Map<String, Int> = map_insert(empty_map(), \"a\", 1)` then `let q: Map<Bool, Bool> = m` compiles with no diagnostic under both `gunbc run` and `gunbc compile --target rust`.",

    "DISTINGUISHING FACTS, two links in one rule chain: v1.compiler.infer declared_type_conformance_diags_core ended `if !both_ground { [] }`, and conformance_ground_type admitted only kernel scalars and element collections whose first element is a kernel scalar, excluding keyed collections by name -- so every Map pair was accepted with no judgment; and v1.compiler.types node_type_compatible's container arm compared `children |> first`, so every argument after the first was never compared even where the pair was judged. The one-peel leaves beside it (declared_type_kernel_inhabitance_mismatch_at_element, callable_element_signature_mismatch) each stated their own depth-one narrowing.",

    "RUNG: found BELOW the ladder -- accepted and emitted with no diagnostic.",

    "CEILING 3, structurally guaranteed: the source can still write the mismatch, and the compiler can refuse every one whose positions are established, because two applications of one template compare positionally on a finite type tree. A position holding an unsolved type variable is not decided by this judgment; it is a counted undecided cause, never an agreement, and a concrete disagreement at a sibling position still refuses.",

    "NEXT-RUNG TRIGGER: v1.compiler.types application_arguments_verdict consumed at v1.compiler.infer declared_type_conformance_diags_core, with the discriminating REDs and paired controls in test.claim.declared_container_argument_witness executed against a seed built from that change. The row is read at the ceiling only once those execute.",

    "REVIEW TELL: a declared-type judgment that reads `children |> first`, peels exactly one level, or excludes a collection kind by name and returns an empty diagnostic list for what it excluded.",
  ],

  evidence: [],
}
